2.0.1:
[Fix] Test suite: CentOS 6 (bash 4.1) compatibility — conditional declare -gA
      fallback in bfd_standard_setup(), bfd_require_bash42() skip guard for
      tests needing string-keyed associative arrays (739 failures → 0)
[Change] bfd.1: add --events option, update --json/--csv scope to -l/-e/-a
[Change] README.md, README: add section 5.8 Events Dashboard; update section
      5.6 Structured Output with events/attackpool examples; add -e to CLI block
[New] search_ip(): live pressure score and per-service pressure breakdown
      shown in unified IP report (text, JSON, CSV)
[New] _apool_report(): PRESSURE column with live per-IP pressure scores
      for attack pool top-25 reports (text, JSON, CSV)
[New] --json/--csv for --events: structured output for events dashboard,
      per-IP detail, and CIDR subnet reports
[New] --json/--csv for -a: structured output for attack pool reports,
      per-service breakdown, and search_ip unified IP reports
[New] _json_array_from_csv(): helper converts comma-separated service lists
      to JSON arrays for structured output
[Change] events_dashboard()/events_cidr() refactored: shared awk helpers
      (_events_dashboard_awk, _events_cidr_awk) for reuse by JSON/CSV variants
[Change] _apool_report() refactored: shared _apool_awk() pipeline for reuse
      by JSON/CSV variants
[Change] usage(): --json/--csv scope expanded from -l to -l, -e, -a
[New] --events: active pressure dashboard showing all tracked IPs with
      pressure scores, event counts, services, and ban proximity
[New] --events IP: per-IP pressure detail with per-service breakdown,
      weights, event counts, and scoring context
[New] --events CIDR: subnet-scoped pressure report for IPv4 (mask 8-32)
      using mawk-compatible CIDR math
[New] validate_cidr(): validates IPv4 CIDR notation (mask 8-32)
[New] verbose pressure: -V shows per-IP pressure score, trip threshold, and
      effective weight during detection cycles; country multiplier arrow when
      weight differs; global pressure ban line when cross-service triggers
[Fix] Dockerfile path alignment: project files now at /opt/ (not /opt/bfd/)
      matching /opt/tests/ test path for correct PROJECT_ROOT resolution
